<body>
<div class="app">
  <header class="topbar">
    <div class="brand"><h1>Strangereal Theatre Log</h1><span id="brand-sub">WAR RECORD · 1995–2040</span></div>
    <nav class="tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="View"><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-theatre" aria-selected="true" aria-controls="theatre">Theatre map</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-hangar" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="hangar">Hangar</button><button type="button" role="tab" id="tab-timeline" aria-selected="false" aria-controls="timeline">Timeline</button></nav>
    <div class="readouts" id="readouts">
      <div>THEATRE <b id="r-theatre">ALL</b></div>
      <div>YEAR <b id="r-year">—</b></div>
      <div>LOGGED <b id="r-logged">0/0</b></div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <aside class="panel tv" aria-label="Wars and games">
    <div class="ph"><span>Operations</span><b>Chronological</b></div>
    <button class="allbtn" id="allbtn" type="button">Show full theatre</button>
    <ul class="missions" id="missions"></ul>
  </aside>

  <main class="mapwrap tv" id="mapwrap">
    <canvas id="gl" aria-label="3D map of Strangereal. Drag to rotate, scroll or pinch to zoom, tap a country marker for its record."></canvas>
    <div id="labels"></div>
    <button class="lmtoggle" id="lmtoggle" type="button" aria-pressed="true">◆ LANDMARKS · ON</button>
    <svg class="reticle" viewBox="0 0 46 46" aria-hidden="true"><g fill="none" stroke="#9fe3ff" stroke-width="1.2"><path d="M4 14V4h10M32 4h10v10M42 32v10H32M14 42H4V32"/><circle cx="23" cy="23" r="2"/></g></svg>
    <div class="hud-corner hud-tl" id="hud-tl">AFTER OFFICIAL AC8 WORLD MAP · STYLISED</div>
    <div class="hud-corner hud-bl legend" aria-label="Legend">
      <span><i style="background:var(--friendly)"></i>PLAYER SIDE</span>
      <span><i style="background:var(--hostile)"></i>HOSTILE</span>
      <span><i style="background:var(--involved)"></i>INVOLVED</span>
    </div>
    <div class="hud-corner hud-br">DRAG · ROTATE<br>SCROLL · ZOOM</div>
  </main>

  <aside class="panel tv" aria-label="Intel">
    <div class="ph"><span id="intel-h">Briefing</span><b id="intel-code">—</b></div>
    <div class="dossier" id="dossier"></div>
  </aside>

  <section id="hangar" aria-label="Hangar: playable aircraft by real-world maker" hidden>
  <div class="controls">
    <input id="q" type="search" placeholder="Search aircraft, e.g. Su-47" aria-label="Search aircraft">
    <div class="seg" id="hview" role="group" aria-label="Hangar view"><button type="button" data-hv="table" aria-pressed="true">By maker</button><button type="button" data-hv="time" aria-pressed="false">By first flight + lineage</button></div>
    <div class="seg" id="horder" role="group" aria-label="Row order" hidden><button type="button" data-ho="date">Rows by date</button><button type="button" data-ho="maker">Rows by maker</button></div>
    <div class="hstats" id="stats"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="mkrow">
  <nav class="chips" id="makers" aria-label="Jump to maker"></nav>
  </div>
  <div class="legend">
    <span><i class="dot"></i>Playable</span>
    <span><i class="dot d"></i>DLC / pre-order</span>
    <span><i class="dot" style="background:var(--orig);box-shadow:none"></i>Strangereal original</span>
    <span>Tap a game column to filter · tap an aircraft to open its file</span>
    <span class="tonly"><i class="lg-line"></i>Developed from</span><span class="tonly"><i class="lg-line" style="border-top:1.5px dashed var(--dlc)"></i>Drew on</span><span class="tonly"><i class="lg-line" style="border-top:1.5px dashed var(--orig)"></i>Fictional derivative</span>
    <span class="status" id="status" aria-live="polite"></span>
  </div>
  <div class="board" id="board"><table id="t"></table></div>
  <div class="tboard" id="tboard" hidden></div>
  <aside class="hdetail" id="hdetail" aria-label="Aircraft details" hidden><div class="hd-top"><span>AIRCRAFT FILE</span><button type="button" class="hd-x" id="hd-close">CLOSE ✕</button></div><div id="hd-body"></div></aside>
  <details class="foot"><summary>About this data</summary>
    <p>Rosters come from each game's aircraft page on the Ace Combat Wiki. Air Combat, Ace Combat 2 and Ace Combat 04 used short in-game names (F-15, EF-2000, TND-IDS, R-M01, SF-39); these are matched to the nearest real variant. SF-35 and SF-39 are read as the Saab Draken and Gripen. Top Gun: Maverick versions of the F-14A and F/A-18E in Ace Combat 7 are folded into those rows.</p>
    <p>Ace Combat 3's corporate-era jets are placed under the real aircraft they descend from. Neucom, Ouroboros and Northern Wings designs have no real maker, so they sit with the other Strangereal originals; Northern Wings notes say which real jet each resembles.</p>
    <p>The first-flight view places real aircraft by the year that variant first flew (c. marks an approximate year), and proposals that were never built at the year they were proposed. Fictional aircraft have no real date, so Strangereal originals and in-game variants sit at the in-universe year of the earliest game they appear in: 1995 for Ace Combat Zero, 2040 for Ace Combat 3. The shaded area past 2026 is the in-game future, and the violet marks on the axis show the year each game is set in. Lines show which aircraft each one was developed from; a hollow grey diamond is a family ancestor that isn't playable. Photos load live from Wikipedia; 3D models are schematics built from each aircraft's wing, tail and engine layout.</p>
  </details>
</section>
  <section id="timeline" aria-label="Strangereal timeline" hidden>
    <div class="tlbar">
      <input id="tlq" type="search" placeholder="Search the timeline, e.g. Excalibur" aria-label="Search timeline">
      <div class="tlchips" id="tlchips" role="group" aria-label="Filter"></div>
      <span class="status" id="tlstatus" aria-live="polite" style="font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)"></span>
    </div>
    <div class="tlscroll" id="tlscroll"></div>
    <details class="foot"><summary>About this data</summary><p>Dates through 1999 follow the Ace Combat Wiki's Strangereal timeline (a condensed reading; minor enlistments and transfers are left out). The wiki page I could reach stops partway through 1999, so entries from 2000 on come from the war briefings in this log rather than the timeline page.</p></details>
  </section>
</div>

