 {id:"ac7",code:"7",title:"Ace Combat 7: Skies Unknown",year:2019,war:"Lighthouse War",kind:"game",player:"Trigger · Spare / Strider (LRSSG)",
  summary:"Under former president Vincent Harling, Osea agreed with Usean nations to build the International Space Elevator, the 'Lighthouse', in the Gunther region, guarded by Osean and IUN forces and the Arsenal Bird flying warships. Radical young officers in Erusea convinced Princess Rosa Cossette D'Elise, and then the royal family, that Osea meant to dominate Usea. Erusea struck first with hidden drones on May 15, 2019. Osea won the war, but a satellite blackout and Erusea's collapse left Usea in chaos, and the final battle was fought by a joint Osean–Erusean force against Erusea's own runaway drone program.",
  cast:[["OSEA","Trigger ('Three Strikes'), former president Vincent Harling"],["ERUSEA","Mihaly A. Shilage ('Mister X'), Princess Rosa Cossette D'Elise, Capt. Matias Torres (Alicorn)"],["EASA","Dr. Schroeder, who helps shut down the drone factories"],["MIMIC","Otto and Elke van Dalsen, assassins hired to kill Trigger"],["DRONES","Hugin and Munin, the ADF-11F Raven pair"]],
  beats:["Before the war: Osea and Usean nations build the space elevator. Erusean Radicals turn the royal family against Osea.",
   "May 15, 2019: Erusea declares war and seizes the Lighthouse. Drones hidden in shipping containers hit Osean ports at Aulick, St. Hewlett, Bana City and Oured, and Erusea takes control of the Arsenal Birds.",
   "Late May: Osea strikes Farbanti from the carrier Kestrel II and retakes the Scofields Plateau airfield. A two-front offensive on May 30 fails; Erusea holds Farbanti and the Chopinburg Rainforest.",
   "Mid-August: The penal Spare Squadron probes Erusea's radar net. The LRSSG wipes out the reserve fleet at Snider's Top, and Stonehenge shoots down the Arsenal Bird Liberty.",
   "Sep 2: The LRSSG stops an Erusean missile launch from Sierraplata.",
   "Sep 4: Osea tries to capture the submersible Alicorn at Artiglio Port. Captain Torres refuses to scuttle it, fires on the landing fleet and escapes.",
   "Sep 10: Strider destroys the port and fleet at Anchorhead. Mimic Squadron's attempt to kill Trigger fails and both van Dalsen siblings die.",
   "Sep 14: The Alicorn is sunk in the Spring Sea, ending its nuclear railgun threat.",
   "Late September: Cape Rainy is captured, and Farbanti falls after a siege.",
   "Late 2019: Anti-satellite strikes by both sides cause a worldwide communications blackout. Erusea's government collapses and breakaway regions such as Shilage declare independence.",
   "Late October: Osean and Erusean forces, refugees, Princess Rosa and EASA staff destroy the Arsenal Bird Justice and the Ravens Hugin and Munin at the Lighthouse. The Radicals surrender.",
   "Dec 1, 2019: A ceasefire from the Expo City Conference ends the war. The Lighthouse returns to IUN control and Rosa forms a provisional government there."],
  roles:{osea:"friendly",erusea:"hostile",usea:"involved",fcu:"involved"},
  events:{osea:"Hit by surprise drone strikes on its home ports. Trigger, accused of killing former president Harling, is sent to the penal Spare Squadron and later flies with Strider in the LRSSG. Osea takes Farbanti in September and wins the war, though its final battle is fought alongside Erusean forces.",
   erusea:"Radical officers win over the royal family and start the war, seizing the Lighthouse and the Arsenal Birds and fielding drone fighters built with EASA and Gründer Industries. After Farbanti falls and the satellite blackout hits, the government collapses and regions like Shilage break away. Radicals keep building drones until a joint force that includes Princess Rosa stops them. Rosa then leads a provisional government based at the Lighthouse.",
   usea:"The Lighthouse in the Gunther region is the prize of the war and the site of its last battle. The satellite blackout throws the continent into chaos, and fighting goes on in Erusea's breakaway regions after the ceasefire.",
   fcu:"Listed among the war's belligerents. The wiki article doesn't detail its part."},
  arcs:[["erusea","osea"],["erusea","usea"]]},
