 {id:"ac8",code:"8",title:"Ace Combat 8: Wings of Theve",year:2029,war:"Sotoa–Usea War",kind:"game",tag:"NEW",player:"Wings of Theve · Joker Flight (carrier Endurance)",
  summary:"Sotoa's rush to industrialize, meant to keep pace with Yuktobania, dried out its land and pushed its generals toward a long-planned invasion of Usea. The FCU was split between a rich west near the space elevator and a poorer east sunk in Sotoan-backed debt, and it was still rearming after IUN peacekeepers left. On July 16, 2029, Sotoa opened the war with a strike from its Tonitrus satellite on Expo City. Behind both sides stood Enso Order, a megacorporation that drew the war out for profit and whose PR arm created the 'Wings of Theve' legend. A treaty ended the fighting on August 3, 2030.",
  cast:[["FCU","Jan 'Rex' Cope (original Wings of Theve), Lucas Díez Doniphan"],["SOTOA","Sabir Kurbanov and Carmille Tewy (Air Force Directors General), Lt. Gen. Daniil Kurbanov"],["LUX LUNAE","Girish Toprak, Ilhan Alem"],["ENSO ORDER","Megacorporation working both sides through Planning Division 303"],["OTHERS","Savia; Newfield Island and Southern Waiapolo separatists; Frente de Liberación partisans; Shilage Volunteer Corps"]],
  beats:["2020–2027: Sotoa routes infrastructure money into eastern Usea and the Eusian Sea through Enso Order, building dependence. Rocky Island becomes a port and shipyard.",
   "Feb 2028: A staged reactor accident on Rocky Island hides construction of the Tonitrus satellite and two land battleships.",
   "Jan 2029: Tonitrus launches from Comona Base, presented to the public as a space telescope.",
   "Jul 16, 2029: Tonitrus strikes Expo City. The land battleships reach the city the next day.",
   "Oct 5, 2029: Theve falls to Sotoa.",
   "Late Oct 2029: Lux Lunae's Girish Toprak kills Rex Cope. The FCU hides his death and his backseater becomes the new Wings of Theve.",
   "Nov 2029: The FCU sinks Sotoa's Third and Fifth Fleets off Newfield Island. A first attempt to retake Theve fails.",
   "Dec 24–26, 2029: Theve is retaken and the land battleship Xanthos is capsized in the city.",
   "Jan 2030: Joker Flight stops parts for a third land battleship. A Tonitrus Spear strike kills about 4,000 civilians in Rio Bajo. Balios launches a second satellite before it is destroyed, and the space elevator is damaged.",
   "Feb 2030: A shuttle from Comona Base cripples Tonitrus No. 2. Expo City is retaken. At Rocky Island, Tonitrus No. 1 is destroyed and both Kurbanov brothers are killed.",
   "Mar–Apr 2030: A costly landing on Cima Island. Megafloat Fatsia falls on April 1, killing many Sotoan warlords. Sotoa's counter-attack on Cima fails and the war is effectively over.",
   "Apr 2030: Enso starts destroying evidence. Carmille Tewy tries to expose Enso by aiming a Tonitrus Spear at Xanthos's reactors and is killed by Joker Flight. Enso sends the submersible Triumphant after Endurance to silence Doniphan.",
   "Late Apr 2030: Doniphan broadcasts proof of Enso's guilt to over 90 million viewers, and 'Wings of Theve' becomes a name known worldwide.",
   "Aug 2030: The FCU and Sotoa sign a treaty on August 3, refusing Enso's mediation. Enso dissolves on August 31 and its assets pass to General Resource."],
  roles:{fcu:"friendly",sotoa:"hostile",usea:"involved",osea:"involved",yuktobania:"involved"},
  events:{fcu:"Loses Expo City, then Theve on October 5, 2029. Flying from the carrier Endurance, Joker Flight and the new Wings of Theve help retake Theve on Christmas Eve, followed by Expo City, Rocky Island and Megafloat Fatsia. Newfield Island and Southern Waiapolo backed Sotoa until April 2030, and Savia switched to the FCU side. After the treaty, several former member states secede.",
   sotoa:"Invades with the Tonitrus satellite and the land battleships Xanthos and Balios. Both battleships and both satellites are destroyed, its fleets and air force are broken, and the fall of Megafloat Fatsia kills many of its warlords. It signs a treaty on August 3, 2030.",
   usea:"About one million people die. The space elevator is badly damaged, rebuilding is expected to run to around 2045, and Usea's refugee population grows several times over. The IUN is reformed as the Neo United Nations.",
   osea:"Stays out of the fighting. Enso Order hoped to drag Osea in, and Osean public opinion was leaning toward intervention by February 2030.",
   yuktobania:"Not a belligerent. Sotoa's industrial push, which set the war in motion, was aimed at keeping up with Yuktobania, and Enso hoped to provoke a Yuktobanian intervention."},
  arcs:[["sotoa","fcu"],["sotoa","usea"]]},
 {id:"ac3",code:"3",title:"Ace Combat 3: Electrosphere",year:2040,war:"Corporate War",kind:"game",player:"Nemo · UPEO SARF",
  summary:"Megacorporations General Resource and Neucom have grown more powerful than nations. After the Faith Park Dispute, UPEO forces destroy a Neucom transport group; Neucom calls the UPEO a General Resource puppet and declares war. The player, Nemo, flies for UPEO's Special Armed Response Force (SARF). The war turns out to be engineered by Ouroboros, a revolutionary group that includes UPEO Supreme Commander Gilbert Park. Later lore frames the whole war as a simulation run inside the Nemo AI program by its creator, Simon Orestes Cohen.",
  cast:[["SARF","Nemo, Rena Hirose, Erich Jaeger, Fiona Chris Fitzgerald"],["GENERAL RES.","Abyssal Dision (top ace, later defects), Keith Bryan"],["NEUCOM","Cynthia Bridgitte Fitzgerald, Fiona's sister"],["UPEO","Gilbert Park (Supreme Commander), Gabriel Clarkson (Representative)"],["OUROBOROS","Revolutionary group behind the war"]],
  beats:["The Faith Park Dispute raises tensions; peace efforts by UPEO and the NUN fail.",
   "SARF destroys a Neucom transport group and Neucom declares war on General Resource.",
   "Neucom jams GR antennas in the Waipolo Mountains; its build-up at Megafloat is broken up.",
   "GR destroys a Neucom ammunition plant and air base; Neucom shifts to high-altitude transports.",
   "The fight reaches orbit over GR's Orbital Satellite Lasers. One is destroyed in space; another falls near Megafloat and Neucom recovers it.",
   "Nanomachines run loose at Neucom's Chopinburg facility and SARF contains them.",
   "GR sinks Neucom's submarine fleet. UPEO's Gabriel Clarkson is shot down, reportedly while defecting to Neucom.",
   "SARF forces a chemical-weapons airship down at Axel Bay. GR raids Megafloat and heavily damages Port Edwards.",
   "Park's link to Ouroboros comes out and SARF breaks from the UPEO to hunt him.",
   "Megafloat is destroyed, Ouroboros's flagship falls, and its remaining forces are lost in the Geofront.",
   "The last duel against Abyssal Dision moves into the Electrosphere, where he is deleted. The game has five endings; Dision dies in all of them.",
   "Late 2040: eight XR-900 Geopelias attack Port Edwards and are destroyed by a hijacked GRDF fighter flown by an AI."],
  factions:[{"n": "UPEO", "tag": "Peacekeepers", "t": "The Universal Peace Enforcement Organization is the Neo United Nations' enforcement arm, created because the NUN could not back up its own orders. It has two halves: SARF, its fighter force, and the Euro-Asia Public Network, a neutral broadcaster. It works out of New Ark Airport in Expo City (earlier from Snider's Top). Its neutrality is thin. General Resource hands it aircraft in the opening missions, and its Supreme Commander, Gilbert Park, used to sit on GR's head staff, which is exactly what Neucom points to when it calls UPEO a GR puppet. The other UPEO leader, Gabriel W. Clarkson, is the ambassador-type figure who brokers the ceasefire and later tries to switch sides. Park is secretly Ouroboros, and uses SARF against wrongly marked targets to keep the two corporations at each other's throats."}, {"n": "SARF", "tag": "Nemo's unit", "t": "The Special Armed Response Force is UPEO's strike wing. Nemo is a rookie in it. Around him: Rena Hirose, a prodigy whose past is tied to Dision in ways she can't remember; Erich Jaeger, who distrusts Park early and stays loyal to Nemo; and Fiona Chris Fitzgerald, whose older sister Cynthia is Neucom's top ace. That last link is what makes the Neucom split personal. SARF flies a mix of Typhoon IIs, MiG-33s, F-16s and Su-37s, and later the Su-43 Berkut."}, {"n": "General Resource", "tag": "Corporation", "t": "General Resource Limited (GR) dominates Usea. Its forces, the GRDF, are led in the air by Abyssal Dision and his wingman Keith Bryan. GR began sanctioning Neucom in 2036 and ran media campaigns against it; armed clashes followed in 2038. Its executive director, Aldair Carlos Nascimento, dies when the control program in his artificial heart fails. The scramble over who succeeds him raises the odds of all-out war with Neucom, and on the routes where Dision walks away from GR, its chain of command falls apart."}, {"n": "Neucom", "tag": "Corporation", "t": "Neucom Incorporated (called Neuwork in the export version) is GR's challenger in communications, software, biotech and aerospace. It finished the floating city Megafloat in 2039, and its fleets gather there. Its fighters operate as the Neucom Emergency Unit, and its ace is Cynthia Bridgitte Fitzgerald. Its research sites include Chopinburg, where a nanomachine outbreak breaks out in the UPEO route. Neucom is the first to declare war, after UPEO strikes one of its transport groups and it decides UPEO is a GR puppet."}, {"n": "Ouroboros", "tag": "Terrorists", "t": "A transhumanist group that believes people can move into the Electrosphere, a networked digital world, and live on there. It calls this sublimation. Its base is the airship Sphyrna. Its leader is Abyssal Dision, or more exactly a digital copy of him: the human Dision died in a 2030 bombing, the same one that killed the researcher Yoko Martha Inoue. Rena flies its Night Raven, whose laser destroys Megafloat, and Dision flies the Aurora. Ouroboros wants to overthrow GR, Neucom and UPEO alike. It lit the fuse of the whole war, and Park is its inside man. Depending on your route, Cynthia may join it too."}, {"n": "Nemo and Simon", "tag": "The truth", "t": "Nemo isn't a man. He is an AI trained by Simon Orestes Cohen, a Neucom researcher who used to work for General Resource. Simon blamed Dision for the 2030 bombing that killed Yoko Martha Inoue, a neuroscientist who studied sublimation (some accounts make her his lover), and built Nemo to destroy the digital Dision. The Intercorporate War is the training run: a simulated war staged in the Electrosphere. Play all five endings and a last scene shows Simon pleased with the result, wiping the data, restarting Nemo and releasing it into the real world. What Nemo does there is never shown."}],opening:"Every route begins the same way. In Awakening, Neucom moves against GR over Faith Park and UPEO sends SARF, with Nemo as its rookie. Bravado has SARF knocking out a Neucom jamming site in the Waiapolo Mountains while GR quietly gives UPEO two fighters, which doesn't look like peacekeeping. In Enter Dision, SARF meets GR's ace Abyssal Dision and his wingman Keith Bryan. In Paper Tiger, SARF and the GRDF pilots hit Neucom's fleet at Megafloat; Clarkson announces a ceasefire mid-mission, and Dision then offers Nemo a place on GR's side. That offer is the first fork.",routes:[{"n": "UPEO", "end": "A Canopy of Stars", "via": "Turn Dision down after Paper Tiger. Later, when Park orders Clarkson's R-505U shot down in Scylla and Charybdis, let it happen (you or Rena fire).", "ms": "Broken Truce · Ghosts of the Past · (No Clearance, if you find the secret base) · Fragile Cargo · Scylla and Charybdis · Fates Intertwined · Reaching for Stars · One-Way Ticket · Bug Hunt · Pawns in the Game · Damage Control · Broken Wings · Sphyrna · A Canopy of Stars", "b": ["GR breaks the ceasefire by hitting a Neucom airbase, so SARF ends up defending Neucom, and Neucom in turn supplies UPEO with jets.", "Nemo and Rena wreck a GR research facility. It stirs Rena's lost memories of Dision and the Night Raven, and she asks Nemo to help her look for it.", "On Clarkson's escort flight, GR ambushes the transport and Park declares that Clarkson and Fiona betrayed UPEO. The aircraft is shot down, killing both. Park is now in control of UPEO.", "Erich and Rena start to doubt him. SARF is sent against both corporations: White Valley, the Comona Islands, the Sandbury Desert, then the Nano-Byte outbreak at Chopinburg, where Nemo saves Rena. Nascimento dies, and Park's plan, to let GR and Neucom wear each other down, comes into focus.", "A false-flag bombing in Expo City pushes the war into an all-out battle over Port Edwards. Ouroboros then launches its Electrosphere attack and names Dision as its leader. Park joins it and invites SARF to follow.", "Rena goes after Dision aboard the Sphyrna; Dision cripples the Night Raven and she crashes. Erich and Nemo shoot down the Sphyrna, killing Dision, then fight through UPEO's own fighters to Park's base and shoot down the Osprey he is fleeing in."], "e": "Park is dead and Rena is found alive on a beach near Expo City. This is the only route where Nemo and Erich finish the job together, and the only one where UPEO is cleaned up from the inside."}, {"n": "General Resource", "end": "Geopelia", "via": "Accept Dision's offer after Paper Tiger. At the Dilemma fork, stay with Keith rather than follow Dision.", "ms": "Soldier of Fortune · Megafloat · (Target Acquisition) · Partners · Tainted Peace · Stratosphere · (Welcoming Committee · Technology Transfer · Claustrophobia) · Dilemma · Betrayal · Heart of the Serpent · (Geofront Attack) · Casualties of War · Geopelia", "b": ["Nemo joins the GRDF. Keith resents the newcomer, but the three of them hit a Neucom airbase in the Waiapolo Mountains despite the ceasefire.", "At Megafloat, if Nemo sinks a fleeing hydrofoil, Dision recovers data on a weapon GR secretly gave UPEO. He then takes Nemo on an unauthorised flight over Expo City, where they run into Rena.", "Dision orders Nemo to shoot down Clarkson's R-505U; Clarkson and Fiona die and GR calls it an accident. Keith warns Nemo that their orders serve Dision's own agenda.", "Neucom hits back at White Valley with high-altitude bombers and parasite fighters. Whether Nemo saves Keith there decides which side missions follow (a Comona Islands and Amber Mountains run, or an assault on a space facility).", "Nascimento dies. Dision reveals he has been sublimated and invites Nemo to help him overthrow all three powers. At the Petrol Coast he announces he is leaving GR; Keith threatens to shoot him down, and Nemo stays with Keith.", "Ouroboros emerges and GR's chain of command collapses. Rena destroys Megafloat with the Night Raven's laser, and Nemo and Keith bring down the Sphyrna. Rena flees into the Geofront under Saint Ark, where Nemo can collapse its installations on her.", "The chase ends over Port Edwards: Nemo shoots down Rena and the Night Raven. Dision appears in the Aurora and Keith gives his life to destroy him."], "e": "Ouroboros collapses and Dision is gone, but Keith and Rena are dead. Eight silver XR-900 Geopelias then attack Port Edwards; Nemo hijacks one and destroys the other seven. GR offers no explanation."}, {"n": "Neucom", "end": "Sole Survivor", "via": "Instead of letting the R-505U be shot down, turn on UPEO's own R-101U fighters so Clarkson's transport gets away (Rena backs off). Later, at Utopian Dreams, stay with Fiona rather than follow Cynthia.", "ms": "Power for Life · (Guardian Angel · Zero Gravity · The Prize) · Utopian Dreams · Resistance · (Radio Silence) · Revenge · Tunnel Vision · Sole Survivor", "b": ["A Neucom flight meets the transport and escorts it home. Clarkson and 38 others defect to Neucom, and Fiona transfers across with Nemo.", "Cynthia, Fiona's sister, leads the unit. The three of them attack White Valley and fly the satellite and orbit missions. Fiona finds Cynthia on a list of sublimation test subjects, and Cynthia admits she volunteered, and joined Neucom to do it.", "Cynthia quietly invites Nemo into her plans. After a raid on a GR airbase, a coup is reported and Cynthia reveals she is part of it. She flies off and leaves Nemo a choice.", "Nemo and Fiona find the Sphyrna with Cynthia over Ouroboros territory and drive the carrier off. The ending stretch plays out one of two ways: either Cynthia fails to answer Fiona's calls and Nemo shoots her down (the hidden mission Radio Silence), or she is presumed to be aboard the Sphyrna when it falls.", "The Night Raven destroys Megafloat. Nemo and Fiona destroy the Sphyrna, and two aircraft escape into the Geofront. On Simon's advice, they hack its aeon generators, which cripples the pair; they shoot down Rena first, then Dision's Aurora. Dision calls out for Yoko as he dies."], "e": "Rena is recovered alive but unresponsive. Fiona announces she is leaving Neucom. Later she gets a message that seems to come from Cynthia, now living digitally, who says she is happy. Fiona breaks down."}, {"n": "Ouroboros (via GR)", "end": "Electrosphere", "via": "Accept Dision's offer, then at the Dilemma fork follow Dision.", "ms": "The Orientation · (Liquidation) · Archnemesis · Memory Error · Electrosphere", "b": ["Nemo follows Dision to the Sphyrna and joins Ouroboros. Rena welcomes him, and Dision claims responsibility for Nascimento's death.", "At Port Edwards Nemo destroys elevated roads, Neucom's headquarters and helicopters carrying its leaders, then chases the survivors to Megafloat and intercepts a large missile. The Night Raven destroys Megafloat. Dision turns on UPEO.", "Nemo regains memories of the experiment that created Dision's copy, and of the bombing that killed Yoko and the human Dision. He and Dision strike UPEO over Expo City and go down into its underground airport, where Dision kills Park. Nemo's contact with Rena restores her memories, and Dision declares Nemo an enemy.", "Over Rocky Island, Keith challenges Dision and fights beside Nemo. Rena's laser damages Keith's fighter; he lodges it in the Night Raven's wing so Nemo can lock on, and asks Nemo to fire. Nemo kills Keith and Rena, then destroys the Sphyrna.", "Nemo chases Dision into the Electrosphere and destroys him there. Dision, struggling with lost memories, recognises Simon's hand in it."], "e": "Investigators find wreckage but no bodies and no survivors, and the coup's circumstances stay unresolved. Keith and Rena are dead, and Megafloat and the Sphyrna are gone."}, {"n": "Ouroboros (via Neucom)", "end": "Self Awareness", "via": "Take the Neucom route, then at Utopian Dreams follow Cynthia.", "ms": "Reality Distortion · Counterrevolution · Pursuit · Self Awareness", "b": ["Nemo follows Cynthia into Ouroboros. A news report says Fiona died in an explosion at a Neucom airbase in the Waiapolo Mountains, and Cynthia blames Neucom and, at first, believes in Dision's cause.", "Dision sends Nemo and Cynthia to seize Rena and the Night Raven from a UPEO base in Expo City. Nemo clears the defences, Cynthia extracts Rena, and Dision gives her the Night Raven.", "Cynthia rejects Dision's use of force. He mocks her ideals, she resolves to leave Ouroboros, and she asks Nemo to help end the fighting.", "They chase Dision towards Megafloat. The Night Raven destroys it; they destroy the Sphyrna, shoot down Dision's Aurora, and Cynthia dedicates the victory to Fiona. Rena runs through the Geofront below Saint Ark; on Simon's advice they destroy the aeon generators and bring her down."], "e": "Cynthia survives. Simon wants to keep her as a test subject and arranges her return to Neucom. She asks Nemo where to go and gets no answer. Neucom, GR and UPEO announce a ceasefire so they can hunt the rebels inside their own ranks. Rena's fate is not stated."}],turning:["Paper Tiger (mission 4): follow Dision, or stay with UPEO.", "The R-505U (mission 9 on the UPEO side): let Clarkson's transport be shot down and stay with UPEO, or turn on your own side's fighters to save it and go to Neucom.", "Dilemma, on the GR side: follow Dision to Ouroboros, or stay with Keith and GR.", "Utopian Dreams, on the Neucom side: follow Cynthia to Ouroboros, or stay with Fiona and Neucom.", "Smaller choices inside missions (saving Keith at White Valley, finding a secret base, how fast you hit a target) open the hidden missions."],
  roles:{usea:"involved"},events:{usea:"The only nation the war record names is Usea, which Neucom set out to shield from General Resource's orbital lasers. The fighting is otherwise told by place, not country: Megafloat, Port Edwards, Chopinburg, Axel Bay, the Comona Islands, the Waipolo Mountains and the Geofront."},arcs:[]}
];

